  set:  # 4d28
    description: "INV-fahub D facet — RE-SCOPED 2026-07-18 to route recovery through the shared receiver-type-index resolver (the family-2 substrate WI), rather than an analyzer-side UFCS resolver. D is the HARDEST/LAST member of that family.\n\nMISBIND (unchanged): d_lang.py confidently misbinds an unresolvable-receiver call (e.g. `thing.exists()`) to an arbitrary same-named internal def: `exists(function)` @0.85. Site: `_resolve_and_emit_call_edge` (d_lang.py:536-584); `resolver.lookup` @563-577; `hints = imported_modules if not receiver else None` @562 DISABLES import-scope disambiguation when a receiver is present; `register_symbol` @667-691 registers every func/method under its bare short name @691, seeding the exact-match.\n\nWHY D IS HARDEST (three compounding D-specifics):\n  1. UFCS — `thing.exists()` may legitimately mean `exists(thing)` (a FREE FUNCTION taking the receiver as first arg), NOT a method on thing's type. A pure suppression gate would kill these; recovery needs first-parameter-type matching, which only the family-2 resolver provides (NOT the inherited_calls MRO walker — that resolves method-on-type only).\n  2. Templates — `arr.map!(fn)` is a template call; `_get_ufcs_template_name` already exists (d_lang.py:518) but first-arg-type matching under generic constraints is harder than plain extension lookup.\n  3. Zero var-type tracking + heavy `auto` — D tracks no receiver types today, and `auto`-inferred receivers give no hint. Needs minimal var-type tracking (param types + typed decls + `auto x = new T()`) to attach a `receiver_type_hint`.\n\nPLAN (after the substrate + the Kotlin validation member land):\n  (a) GATE: a variable receiver that is neither a known module nor a tracked type -> withhold the confident bare-name match; emit py.py's unresolved shape (calls, dst=d:external:0-0:{name}:unresolved, is_resolved=False, evidence_type=ast_call -> 0.40, meta={call_construct:method, +receiver_type_hint when typeable}).\n  (b) VAR-TYPE TRACKING: build minimal receiver typing so the gate can attach a hint (else ~100% of the funnel goes external with zero recovery — the maximal dead-code FP spike; this is why naked D suppression was rejected 2026-07-18).\n  (c) RECOVERY via the family-2 resolver's UFCS branch: match a free function whose FIRST-PARAMETER TYPE == the receiver type before binding; emit `calls` is_resolved=True evidence_type=ast_call_ufcs. Also add `d` to inherited_calls Site-2 for the true method-on-type case (Step-1 direct).\n\nDEPENDS ON: the family-2 substrate WI + the Kotlin validation member (do the clean, template-free member first). INV-fahub D funnel: exists/startsWith/toString @0.85 (verified on current code 2026-07-17). Recall-regression severity if shipped naked: WORST. Tests: family-2 linker template (lang=d, UFCS branch) + d_lang.py producer test (gate + var-type + template)."  # 4d28
